# Camera IDs = video titles

The camera id is the P-code (or Goal id) **in the filename**. Do not assign a file to a different camera because the still “looks like” another view.

## Match 3 (`data/raw/Match 3/`)

| File | Camera |
|------|--------|
| `P1-006.mp4` | **P1** |
| `P6-003.mp4` | **P6** |
| `P7-001.mp4` | **P7** |
| `p8-005.mp4` | **P8** |
| `P9-004.mp4` | **P9** |
| `P10-002.mp4` | **P10** |
| `P_Goal1-007.mp4` | **P_Goal1** |
| `P_Goal2-008.mp4` | **P_Goal2** |

## Match 2

`Cam 3-P1.mp4` → P1, `Cam 8-P10-003.mp4` → P10. Same rule: the P-code in the title is the id.

## If a still seems wrong

Move the **diagram chip** or fix landmarks. **Never** swap files across ids (e.g. do not map `P1-006.mp4` → P9).

Parser: `scripts/gold_set/raw_cam_id.py`. Doc: `docs/product/MATCH3_CAPTURE.md`. Pitch meters: `docs/product/PITCH1_DIMENSIONS.md`.
